## What it owns

TODO. The design doc is `docs/architecture/services/<%= name %>.md` and the OpenAPI stub is
`docs/architecture/openapi/<%= name %>.yaml` — **contracts first** (AGENTS.md §5.1): the stub is written
before or with each route, and `npm run api:types` projects it for Studio once it is in `SPECS`.

## Run

```sh
npx nx test @atlas/<%= name %>        # in memory, no infrastructure
npm run k8s:up                          # builds atlas/<%= name %>:dev and deploys it with the rest
kubectl -n atlas logs deployment/<%= name %> -f
```

Reachable inside the cluster as `http://<%= name %>:3000`. To route it through the gateway, add a row to
the routing table in `apps/api-gateway/src/routing.ts` — and, once it is proxied, a probe for it in
the smoke suite's upstream gate (`infra/smoke/smoke.test.mjs`).

## Configuration

| Variable | Default | |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` / `HOST` | `3000` / `0.0.0.0` | |
| `ATLAS_IAM_ORIGIN` | `http://iam:3000` | Critical readiness dependency |<% if (db) { %>
| `ATLAS_PG_URL` | `postgres://…@postgres:5432/atlas` | Waited for at startup, within a 120 s budget |<% } %><% if (broker) { %>
| `ATLAS_NATS_URL` | `nats://nats:4222` | Retried, never a readiness check |<% } %>
| `ATLAS_OTLP_ENDPOINT` | _(unset: no export)_ | ADR-0004 |
